    {
      "title": "‘We execute the prick’: wife can’t say if Charles Perrottet text was plotting downfall of NSW Liberal minister, Icac hears",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/icac-hears-charles-perrottet-plotted-downfall-nsw-liberal-minister-david-elliott-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Brother of former state premier sent message to wife Anita Perrottet seemingly regarding plan to damage career of rival David Elliott</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/28/nepal-floods-australians-missing-penny-wong-anthony-albanese-angus-taylor-liberal-party-pauline-hanson-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Charles Perrottet wrote about a plan to damage a Liberal minister’s career following his brother’s accession to the New South Wales premiership in October 2021, stating “we execute the prick once party room is over”, a corruption inquiry has heard.</p><p>Anita Perrottet told the Independent Commission Against Corruption (Icac) on Friday she could not recall the meaning of messages exchanged between herself and husband Charles Perrottet in the days before Dominic Perrottet was elected premier by Liberal MPs following the resignation of Gladys Berejiklian.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/icac-hears-charles-perrottet-plotted-downfall-nsw-liberal-minister-david-elliott-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-28T06:02:58"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dolphin dies from H5 bird flu in SA as researchers withdrawn from sub-Antarctic island over ‘psychosocial risk’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/aug/28/dolphin-dies-from-h5-bird-flu-in-sa-as-researchers-withdrawn-from-sub-antarctic-island-over-psychosocial-risk",
      "description": "<p>Expeditioners at research station on Macquarie Island will be evacuated over possible ‘psychological stress’, while 100 dead little penguins found on Tasmanian island</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A dolphin has died from H5 bird flu in South Australia, marking the second native mammal species known to have contracted the virus.</p><p>On Friday afternoon, the Tasmanian government said it was assessing the discovery of about 100 dead little penguins on King Island but it was unable to test them for H5 bird flu due to their “decayed condition”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/aug/28/dolphin-dies-from-h5-bird-flu-in-sa-as-researchers-withdrawn-from-sub-antarctic-island-over-psychosocial-risk\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-28T05:40:40"
    },
    {
      "title": "Identity of high-profile Queensland man drawn into extortion case to remain secret after court ruling",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/identity-of-high-profile-queensland-man-drawn-into-extortion-case-to-remain-secret-after-court-ruling-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Man – referred to as MM by court – will keep his identity hidden after legal challenge against suppression dismissed</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The identity of a high-profile Queensland man drawn into a Cairns extortion case will remain secret, after the state’s supreme court threw out a legal challenge against a suppression order.</p><p>The man – referred to as MM by the court – was <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jun/08/queensland-high-profile-man-extortion-case-name-suppressed-ntwnfb\">drawn into an extortion case earlier this year</a>. He is not a party to the case and is not accused of any offence.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/identity-of-high-profile-queensland-man-drawn-into-extortion-case-to-remain-secret-after-court-ruling-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
